      "description": "Works of Juste-Aurele Meissonier (Oeuvre de Juste- AurPle Meissonier), plate 115: Silver Sculptural Project for a Large Centerpiece and Two Tureens Which Have Been Executed for His Lordship the Duke of Kingston, plate 115 from Works of Juste-Aurèle Meissonier (Oeuvre de Juste-Aurèle Meissonier), c. 1735–37. Gabriel Huquier (French, 1695–1772), after Juste-Aurèle Meissonnier (French, 1695–1750). Etching; sheet: 42 x 66.8 cm (16 9/16 x 26 5/16 in.); platemark: 38 x 64 cm (14 15/16 x 25 3/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, John L. Severance Fund 2000.76",
